!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-order-picks.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A schema whose record `order_pick` holds a value by name: its field `which` is typed `order_ref`,
  `meta.ref<order>`, a reference over a record type, so it names a value of `order` ([TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, §5.12);
  `defaulted_pick`'s field writes the same reference inline and defaults to `o1`. The schema holds such values as
  entries: `o1`, a value of `order`; `r1`, a value of `rush_order`, a subtype of `order`; `c1`, a value of
  `customer`, which is no `order`; and `book`, a value of the namespace type `orders`, whose keys hold values of
  `order`, so `book.first` names one. An entry built with a record type or a namespace type is a value, not a type,
  and a processor that binds binds each to a host class of its own: the records `order`, `rush_order` and
  `customer`.
  """
!schema {
  order          => { id: text }
  rush_order     => order & { by: text }
  customer       => { name: text }
  orders         => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: order }
  order_ref      => meta.ref<order>
  order_pick     => { which: order_ref }
  defaulted_pick => { which?: meta.ref<order> ~ o1 }
  o1             => !order { id: "A-1" }
  r1             => !rush_order { id: "R-1"  by: noon }
  c1             => !customer { name: Ada }
  book           => !orders { first => { id: "B-1" } }
}
